<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson eyes yr-end positive cash flow.</title>
<headline>Ericsson eyes yr-end positive cash flow.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group Ericsson said on Friday it hoped its cash flow would swing from negative to positive towards the end of the year.</p>
<p>&quot;Our cash flow was negative in the first quarter, but we have hopes of it turning toward (positive) the end of the year,&quot; chief financial officer Carl Wilhelm Ros told the annual general meeting.</p>
<p>The company reported earlier that first quarter pre-tax profit rose 30 percent to 2.02 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Joel Dahlberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
